:INHERIT placed after a method, at the bottom of the class
(diag.inherit_position, error). Base:Init() still sees the :INHERIT, so
base_requires_inherit must not also fire.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Panel;
:DECLARE sCaption;

:PROCEDURE Init;
	Base:Init();
	Me:sCaption := "Panel";
:ENDPROC;

:INHERIT Lab.Control;
-- format --
:CLASS Panel;
:DECLARE sCaption;

:PROCEDURE Init;
	Base:Init();
	Me:sCaption := "Panel";
:ENDPROC;

:INHERIT Lab.Control;
-- diagnostics --
9:1-9:9 error inherit_position: ':INHERIT' must directly follow the ':CLASS' statement
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
9:1-9:9 error inherit_position: ':INHERIT' must directly follow the ':CLASS' statement
